fresh-eyes: two independent cold reviewers (subagents, no authorship of this branch), one on the pack writer, one on the cache-key and sweep commits. Both LAND.

Two rounds each. Both found the branch RED where the author reported
green: a new test spawned git, which this crate forbids and its own
integration test enforces, and the author had read the lib target's
count while tests/single_binary failed.

Pack reviewer, round one: write_pack opened the source odb at
git_dir()/objects, so a linked worktree source failed to mirror at
all — a regression this branch introduced, and every worktree in this
project is such a source. common_dir is the same path for an ordinary
repository. Round two: the corrupt-pack test built its own options and
pinned gix-pack rather than this crate, so switching iteration_mode at
the production site kept all 210 green. One constructor now serves
both, and that mutation turns the test red.

Mutations killed, each by a named test: pack skipped on create; ids
collected and dropped; common_dir reverted to git_dir; the source
exists check removed; Verify to Restore at the production site. The
reviewer proved the corrupt-pack assertion fires on the flipped entry
and not the trailer, by recomputing the trailer and seeing Verify
still refuse. The options extraction was proved pure by comparing all
six fields, and the produced packs are byte-identical at 4,064,751 and
908,110 bytes.

Cache-key reviewer, round one: the author's kill claim for the
no-slash condition was false — it held before the colon condition
existed and was never re-run after — and losing it re-collapses two
absolute paths onto one slot. The sweep's prefix test had no coverage,
and the mutant dropping it deletes every entry in the cache root older
than an hour, which is every other store a person has cached. Four
changelog statements were wrong. Round two confirmed all three fixed
and no previously-killed mutant regressed.

Four survivors remain in the walk rewrite, each a partial revert of
one expression pinned twice over elsewhere; judged coverage depth,
not a gate.

210 lib tests, tests/single_binary green, clippy and fmt clean, and
zettel, tisket and almanac all pass against this tree.

Deferred with reviewer assent: the .keep file left in every slot, a
pre-existing nested-tag case identical in both paths, the OOM-abort
path, and deltas not carried, which the changelog states with its 11x
measurement.
